==Trivia==
*Z-Onel's Japanese name, クオリネン ''Kuorinemu'' (Kuolinem), may be derived from クリオネ ''kurione'' ([[wikipedia:Clione|clione]]), レクイエム ''rekuiemu'' (requiem) and 眠る ''nemuru'' (to sleep; can also be used figuratively to mean "to die", i.e., to be laid to rest).
*Her gender is confirmed by the [[media:Death Angel Z-Onel - Phantom Cat.png|event poster]] for [[Last of the Dead (Merciless)|Z-Onel Rises!]], which says, "Can you send this undying terror to her eternal rest?!"
*Among the Tier 2 [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]], Death Angel Z-Onel appears to represent the virtue of charity, which includes self-sacrifice and putting others (her children) above oneself.
*She can be seen as a foil to [[Cruel Angel Clionel]]. Where Clionel is a heavenly [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] who brings destruction, Z-Onel is an unholy [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] who has experienced extinction.
*"Don't come near me or my sons ever again" is a reference to the meme [https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/dont-talk-to-me-or-my-son-ever-again Don't Talk To Me Or My Son Ever Again].
*Like Cruel Angel Clionel, Death Angel Z-Onel makes a few references to ''[[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]'':
**The crosses that appear when she attacks are similar to the [[:Category:EVA Angel Enemies|Angels]]' death effect.
**[[Last of the Dead (Merciless)|Last of the Dead]]'s Japanese name, Saigo no Shisha (最後の死者, lit. "The Final Dead Person"), sounds identical to the Japanese title of ''[[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]'' [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Episode_24 Episode 24]; the only difference is that unlike this stage's name, the episode title spells ''Shisha'' as シ者, allowing it to be interpreted as either "The Final Dead Person" or "The Final Messenger". This wordplay is used in Cruel Angel Clionel's Japanese description as well.
***[[The Final Corpse (Merciless)|The Final Corpse]]'s Japanese name is also Saigo no Shisha (最後の屍者, "The Final Corpse"), except with ''Shisha'' (死者, dead person) spelled as 屍者, replacing the kanji 死 (death) with 屍 (corpse).
**[[With Sympathy (Merciless)|With Sympathy]]'s Japanese name, Magokoro o Neko ni (まごころをネコに, "Sincerely the Cat's"), is a reference to ''Magokoro o, Kimi ni'' (まごころを、君に, "Sincerely Yours"), which is the Japanese title of both ''[[wikipedia:Flowers for Algernon|Flowers for Algernon]]'' and [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Episode_26%27 Episode 26'] of ''Neon Genesis Evangelion''.
*She has the longest range and shortest revive time of all [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]].
*She stands from a range of 666, commonly recognized as the "[[wikipedia:Number of the Beast|Number of the Beast]]".

